{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2c24a8e0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Reproduce Natalie first, then audit each change\n",
    "This notebook starts from Natalie's saved per-frame profiles and reproduces **24.90 Å WT / 30.78 Å AA**. It then changes one choice at a time. The source notebooks and HDF5 files are not modified. Frames and q indices are zero based, with both endpoints included.\n",
    "\n",
    "A changed fit convention is a methodological choice, not evidence that Natalie's result is wrong. q-range sensitivity, background covariance, and a newly selected window must be distinguished. P(r) and Guinier estimates are compared separately."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "fd79062c",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-21T20:18:01.995058Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-21T20:18:01.994789Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.511141Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.510700Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import sys, json, hashlib\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, Markdown, Image\n",
    "ROOT=Path.cwd()\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'analysis'))\n",
    "from inspect_data import load, correct\n",
    "from select_windows import average\n",
    "from run_efa import guinier\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9c8e1aec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Data provenance and exact averaging\n",
    "The saved DAT files contain Natalie’s processed intensities and errors. An arithmetic mean has variance sum(sigma²)/n² when frames are treated as independent; we first reproduce that convention."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "7136ec2b",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.512433Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.512348Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.517927Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.517596Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "WT_092025 frames 175 185 number 11\n",
      "AA_052026 frames 172 182 number 11\n",
      "All input file hashes retained in results/reproduction_input_hashes.json\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "saved={}; hashes={}\n",
    "for name,a,b in [('WT_092025',175,185),('AA_052026',172,182)]:\n",
    "    paths=[ROOT/'BNL_SAXS/dat_files'/name/f'profile_{j}.dat' for j in range(a,b+1)]\n",
    "    d=np.array([np.loadtxt(p) for p in paths])\n",
    "    saved[name]=(d[0,:,0],d[:,:,1].mean(0),np.sqrt((d[:,:,2]**2).sum(0))/len(d))\n",
    "    for p in paths: hashes[str(p.relative_to(ROOT))]=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n",
    "    print(name, 'frames',a,b,'number',len(d))\n",
    "print('All input file hashes retained in results/reproduction_input_hashes.json')\n",
    "(ROOT/'results/reproduction_input_hashes.json').write_text(json.dumps(hashes,indent=2));\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "359e0f60",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Show the fit equation and reproduce the reported values\n",
    "$$y_i=\\ln I_i=a+bq_i^2,\\quad \\sigma_{y_i}=\\sigma_{I_i}/I_i,$$\n",
    "$$\\hat\\beta=(X^TWX)^{-1}X^TWy,\\quad R_g=\\sqrt{-3b},\\quad I(0)=e^a.$$\n",
    "This is RAW's error-weighted linear Guinier fit. The uncertainty below is the conditional covariance error; RAW can additionally report the larger fit-range variation error. WT uses q indices 3–45; AA uses 3–41, verified against saved notebook outputs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "22c5aaa6",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.519006Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.518950Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.521360Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.521059Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "WT_092025 {'Rg': 24.904143040206478, 'fit_se': 0.4967861438280373, 'qmin': 0.009, 'qmax': 0.052, 'qRgmax': 1.2950154380907368, 'chi2': 1.0795553966408564, 'I0': 0.6958219904774279}\n",
      "AA_052026 {'Rg': 30.78492263777366, 'fit_se': 0.11899073791382031, 'qmin': 0.008, 'qmax': 0.046, 'qRgmax': 1.4161064413375883, 'chi2': 2.1558756367660905, 'I0': 5.242626879569802}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def fixed_fit(q,I,E,lo,hi):\n",
    "    m=(q>=lo-1e-12)&(q<=hi+1e-12)&(I>0)&(E>0)\n",
    "    X=np.column_stack([np.ones(m.sum()),q[m]**2]); y=np.log(I[m]); sigma=E[m]/I[m]\n",
    "    cov=np.linalg.inv(X.T@((1/sigma**2)[:,None]*X))\n",
    "    beta=cov@(X.T@(y/sigma**2)); rg=np.sqrt(-3*beta[1])\n",
    "    return dict(Rg=float(rg),fit_se=float(3*np.sqrt(cov[1,1])/(2*rg)),\n",
    "                qmin=float(q[m][0]),qmax=float(q[m][-1]),qRgmax=float(q[m][-1]*rg),\n",
    "                chi2=float(np.sum(((y-X@beta)/sigma)**2)/(len(y)-2)),I0=float(np.exp(beta[0])))\n",
    "reproduced={}\n",
    "for name,end,target in [('WT_092025',45,24.90414304),('AA_052026',41,30.78492264)]:\n",
    "    q,I,E=saved[name]; f=fixed_fit(q,I,E,q[3],q[end]); reproduced[name]=f\n",
    "    assert abs(f['Rg']-target)<1e-6\n",
    "    print(name, f)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
