  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a4071f0e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Observe q-range sensitivity directly\n",
    "The data and errors are unchanged across each curve below. Curvature outside the lowest-q regime can change the fitted slope, particularly for the expanded AA sample. Shorter fits also have larger statistical uncertainty."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "7790dcd5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.587264Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.587166Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.811623Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-21T20:18:02.811187Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1100x800 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig,axes=plt.subplots(2,2,figsize=(11,8))\n",
    "for col,name in enumerate(saved):\n",
    "    q,I,E=saved[name]; ref=reproduced[name]; narrow=guinier(q,I,E)\n",
    "    m=(q>=.008)&(q<=.06)&(I>0)\n",
    "    ax=axes[0,col]; ax.errorbar(q[m]**2,np.log(I[m]),yerr=E[m]/I[m],fmt='.',alpha=.7,color='black')\n",
    "    for f,label in [(ref,'Natalie reproduction'),(narrow,'Conservative qRg≤1')]:\n",
    "        x=np.array([f['qmin'],f['qmax']])**2\n",
    "        ax.plot(x,np.log(f['I0'])-f['Rg']**2*x/3,label=f\"{label}: {f['Rg']:.2f} Å\")\n",
    "    ax.set(title=name,xlabel='q² (Å⁻²)',ylabel='ln I'); ax.legend(fontsize=8)\n",
    "    ends=q[(q>=.026)&(q<=.055)]; fits=[fixed_fit(q,I,E,q[3],end) for end in ends]\n",
    "    axes[1,col].errorbar(ends,[f['Rg'] for f in fits],yerr=[f['fit_se'] for f in fits],fmt='o-',markersize=3)\n",
    "    axes[1,col].set(xlabel='Upper fit q (Å⁻¹)',ylabel='Guinier Rg (Å)',title='Same average, changing upper q only')\n",
    "fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(ROOT/'poster_results/Rg_reproduction_and_qrange.png',dpi=200)\n",
    "display(fig);plt.close(fig)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "30813d7b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. P(r) is a separate estimate\n",
    "Natalie's supplied poster reports GNOM Rg **27.3 Å WT / 34.23 Å AA**, with Dmax **95 / 139 Å**. Our current BIFT estimates are about **27.22 / 34.60 Å** with Dmax **94 / 159 Å**. The AA Guinier discrepancy is largely reproduced by changing the fitted q range on the *same data*. The P(r) Rg estimates are already close, but the AA Dmax difference remains material. GNOM and BIFT regularization/Dmax selection differ; neither should be silently substituted for the other. We have not rerun GNOM or established a unique AA Dmax.\n",
    "\n",
    "A 35 Å Rg is not by itself evidence of oligomerization in an IDR. The size of this sequence must be assessed with the full scattering curve, concentration behavior, uncertainty and ideally an independent mass measurement. No window was selected by closeness to a desired Rg.\n",
    "\n",
    "## New report context\n",
    "WT_raw_report.pdf records buffer frames 210–239 plus a linear baseline using 0–10 and 439–449; this differs from the source DAT correction (220–236). Its four proposed component intervals overlap strongly; the report does not display recovered component curves. AA_raw_report.pdf shows a three-component rotation over 117–250, including q out to 3.19 Å⁻¹; two recovered curves are very noisy. These are analysis settings/results, not proof of four WT or three AA biological species. Notebook 03 checks their sensitivity."
   ]
  }
